            <ArticleTitle>Thermoresponsive cyclodextrins with benzenesulfonamide showing tunable inhibition for carbonic anhydrase.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>8028-8031</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c7ob02171b</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Monodisperse thermoresponsive cyclodextrins appended with benzenesulfonamides were demonstrated to reversibly regulate the enzymatic activity of carbonic anhydrase, which was found to be dependent on both scaffold effect and thermoresponsiveness.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
